Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.17,0:00:03.07,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Episode 47: Two thousand years without
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.52,0:00:08.87,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}On Friday morning Alcyoneus hunted the campus for her in daylight, building by building.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.17,0:00:14.92,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He went out of the faculty hall at first light, past the guard asleep in his car, and nobody stopped him.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.92,0:00:24.26,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He went into the library, ducking under its door, and walked the length of every row of shelves while a woman at the desk held a telephone to her ear and said nothing into it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.52,0:00:35.90,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He went through a building full of glass jars and dead insects pinned in boxes, and a building where young men sat in rows in front of lit screens, all of whom stood up and pressed themselves against the walls as he went by.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.90,0:00:42.57,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He went into the canteen and stood among the steaming trays, breathing in, because she might have left a smell there as she had on the hills.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.89,0:00:43.53,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She hadn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.53,0:00:45.41,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Nobody had seen a woman in grey.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.41,0:00:47.75,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Nobody had seen anything but him.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.07,0:00:51.27,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}So he went back to the one place where he had heard her breathe.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.27,0:00:56.29,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Strings in an old wood had breathed in a rhythm he knew, and it was all he had.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.59,0:00:58.78,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The conservator let him in this time.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.78,0:01:08.22,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She opened the door at his knock and looked up at him for a moment, and then stood aside without a word and went back to her bench, the way she would have let in a colleague with a box to sign for.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.22,0:01:11.12,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He came in bent double under the ceiling.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.37,0:01:13.34,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The professor was there before him.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.62,0:01:20.78,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He sat on a tall stool beside the conservator's bench with his stick leaning against his knee, and he was asking her a question about the humidity in the room.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.78,0:01:25.56,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She answered it as she worked, without looking up, the way you answer a question you are asked every morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.56,0:01:26.72,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She told him the number.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.72,0:01:29.31,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He thanked her for it, and nodded, and didn't write it down.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.31,0:01:31.74,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Alcyoneus saw that he didn't need it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.00,0:01:37.97,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"I've checked the lyre," the conservator said to the giant, in her own speech, and the professor put it into the old tongue for him.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.97,0:01:40.08,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"Twice yesterday and once this morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.08,0:01:41.19,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Nothing's changed.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.19,0:01:42.98,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The strings are where they were."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.98,0:01:50.34,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She lifted the lid of a grey box on the bench and showed him the lyre lying on its foam, and it was only an old instrument, with nothing breathing in it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.62,0:01:55.04,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He looked at it, and then he stopped looking at it, and looked at the professor instead.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.29,0:01:57.39,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The professor was watching her hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.67,0:02:01.16,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He watched them the way a man watches a fire he has been told he mustn't touch.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.16,0:02:07.89,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She was lifting something small out of a tray with a pair of tweezers, a flake of painted plaster no bigger than a fingernail, and setting it on a glass slide.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.89,0:02:12.22,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Her hands were quick and sure in their blue gloves, and the professor's eyes went with them everywhere they went.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.22,0:02:17.25,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}When she turned the slide under the lamp, his face changed a little, and when she set it down it changed back.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.59,0:02:20.07,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Alcyoneus had seen that look before.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.07,0:02:28.69,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He had worn it himself, on the plain, in the long years before the war, every time a woman at the edge of the field had looked at him across the dust.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.99,0:02:36.17,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The conservator got up and went to a tall cabinet at the far end of the room, and bent to the lowest drawer, with her back to them.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.47,0:02:40.22,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"You love her," Alcyoneus said to the professor, in the old tongue.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.22,0:02:43.97,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He said it plainly, as he would have said the sky was clear.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.22,0:02:45.87,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The professor didn't move.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.17,0:02:50.42,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He had gone two thousand years without, Alcyoneus thought, looking at him.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.42,0:02:54.43,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}It was written on him the way age was written on the old man with the ring.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.43,0:02:58.07,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}A man didn't look at a woman's hands like that the first time he loved.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.07,0:03:02.72,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He looked like that when it was the first time and he had waited much too long for it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.97,0:03:04.82,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The professor didn't deny it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.09,0:03:08.27,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"Please," he said, very low, without turning his head.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.27,0:03:10.58,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"Don't say it in a language she understands.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.58,0:03:12.16,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She reads the old texts.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.16,0:03:15.24,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She knows more of that tongue than she lets on."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.50,0:03:16.94,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"Then she should hear it."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.19,0:03:18.09,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"No."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.42,0:03:21.68,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"I loved once where it was forbidden," Alcyoneus said.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.68,0:03:25.21,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"I said nothing, and she said nothing, and the gods said a great deal.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.21,0:03:29.00,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}All that came of keeping quiet was a long time in the clay."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.00,0:03:30.77,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He watched the woman at the cabinet.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.77,0:03:32.52,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"You should tell her."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.77,0:03:34.27,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"I can't," the professor said.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.27,0:03:36.07,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"You don't know what I carry."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.40,0:03:39.66,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The conservator came back with a folder and sat down.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.66,0:03:48.40,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She looked from one of them to the other, a little sharply, as if she had heard the shape of the talk if not the words, and then she opened the folder and began to read it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.69,0:03:54.37,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Alcyoneus sat on the floor with his back against the shelves, and his knees up, and asked them both.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.67,0:03:57.09,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"You keep the old things," he said to her.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.09,0:03:58.90,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"And you tell the old stories."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.90,0:04:00.04,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}That was to him.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.04,0:04:01.15,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"Then tell me this.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.15,0:04:02.65,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Where does a Muse go, to fade?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.65,0:04:03.29,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Not the wood.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.29,0:04:03.97,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The place.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.97,0:04:06.12,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Where does she go at the end?"
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.40,0:04:08.54,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The professor put it into her speech.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.54,0:04:11.97,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The conservator looked up from the folder and shook her head.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.22,0:04:13.89,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"I don't know what he means," she said.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.89,0:04:14.44,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"Go where?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.44,0:04:15.31,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Tell him I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.31,0:04:16.39,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}I don't."
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.64,0:04:18.52,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"I don't know," the professor said.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.82,0:04:20.72,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}This time Alcyoneus heard it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.72,0:04:26.35,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He heard it as clearly as he had heard it on the stubble a week ago, the stone turning under the foot, only louder.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.35,0:04:27.69,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The small man knew.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.69,0:04:35.22,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He had known on the plain and he knew now, sitting on his stool with his eyes on the woman's hands, and he was choosing every minute not to say.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.52,0:04:41.37,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Alcyoneus leaned forward, and spoke low in the old tongue, so that it was between the two of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.64,0:04:42.78,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"A trade," he said.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.78,0:04:44.19,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"I'll keep your secret from her.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.19,0:04:46.97,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}I won't say a word of it, in any speech she has.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.97,0:04:47.94,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}And you give me mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.94,0:04:49.57,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Where is she?"
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.87,0:04:53.44,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The professor looked at him then, for the first time since he had come in.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.44,0:05:00.24,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}His face was more tired than it had been on the plain, and something in it had set hard, like clay in a kiln.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.49,0:05:01.74,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"No," he said.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.99,0:05:03.82,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"You would sooner I told her?"
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.09,0:05:08.87,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"I'd sooner you told her," the professor said, "than I sent you where you want to go."
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.17,0:05:12.48,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He held the giant's eyes while he said it, and didn't look away.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.48,0:05:14.92,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Alcyoneus had seen few mortals do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.92,0:05:17.17,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}He had seen fewer gods.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.44,0:05:19.36,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}The conservator had stopped reading.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.36,0:05:21.19,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}She was looking at the window.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.47,0:05:30.09,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}"Those are ours," she said, in her own speech, and this time the professor didn't need to translate, because Alcyoneus had turned and seen them too.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.42,0:05:39.14,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Out on the road behind the conservation building a white van was drawn up on the verge with the security firm's name along its side, and its door was sliding open.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.14,0:05:40.84,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}Six men were getting out of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.84,0:05:48.54,Default,,90,90,0,,{\an5}They wore black and they had helmets, and they were lifting long clear shields down out of the back one after another and buckling them on their arms.
